{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/206438-recruiting-supernaurals","id":206438,"title":"Recruiting Supernaurals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-23T12:27:51-07:00","id":206438,"title":"Recruiting Supernaurals?","content":"Has anybody played a game where the Hunters decided to recruit non-hostile supernaturals to there cause. For example, the Hunters learn some Changeling and Mage lore and try to get help from the Free Counsel or the Scarecrow Ministry.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thank-you ahead of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T22:34:11-07:00","id":206778,"title":"","content":"My favorite hunter, Eli, once made a deal with a few vampires but it was a short term thing. I think the best hunters and supernaturals can do is a truce, not a permanent peace, but a &quot;Let's not kill each other until the far worse thing is dealt with&quot; or a &quot;This is my neighborhood, and if you mess with it, or I catch you in it, I'll kill you&quot; sort of deal. Any Hunter who knows what a Changeling, Mage, or other supernatural can do likely won't trust them to play fair; any supernatural who knows how limited a Hunter's power is will likely try and manipulate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T23:17:59-07:00","id":206787,"title":"","content":"I'd love to do a game where the cell has to work alongside the Legacy of the Black Apple to keep one of the True Fae appeased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T08:21:16-07:00","id":207105,"title":"","content":"The main Hunter game I played ended up with the hunter being more negotiator in various situations both within a supernatural group and between them. THey ended up making friends with a pack of werewolves, the founders of a faction krewe and a rebellious cult krewe, some changeling nobles, and a couple of other things aside. Hell, even the hardline, monstrous sheriff they pissed off ended up in a knife-at-each-others-throats do-favors-for-each-other sort of relationship.<br /> <br /> This meant that they often went running into situations with monsters way more than they did other humans-in fact, they never did run with straight-up humans.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and in case anyone was thinking, yes, all that friend making was going to bite them in the ass at some point in time. Not everyone they befriended was willing to put practicality behind emotional ties.<br /> <br /> The best part was that it was going to be a demon who made them realize it, with no other intention than doing the hunters(and the people they affiliated with) a favor by not passing a huge bomb around anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-24-2014, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T14:28:27-07:00","id":207527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/206438-recruiting-supernaurals?p=206778#post206778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite hunter, Eli, once made a deal with a few vampires but it was a short term thing. I think the best hunters and supernaturals can do is a truce, not a permanent peace, but a &quot;Let's not kill each other until the far worse thing is dealt with&quot; or a &quot;This is my neighborhood, and if you mess with it, or I catch you in it, I'll kill you&quot; sort of deal. Any Hunter who knows what a Changeling, Mage, or other supernatural can do likely won't trust them to play fair; any supernatural who knows how limited a Hunter's power is will likely try and manipulate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eli &quot;The one who was killed by his own Cell&quot;? His Vigil just sounds like it was full of great decisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:11:01-07:00","id":207915,"title":"","content":"He was my response to a play group that likes to debate for whole sessions on what to do. We'd take 3 hours to figure out how we were going to gather information. Eli said &quot;screw it&quot; and cut to the chase.<br /> <br /> On point, it is possible, I just don't think it would last 5 minutes before either side began trying to figure out how best to ruin/use/kill the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T10:25:58-07:00","id":208441,"title":"","content":"Changelings, Mages, and Demons are the most likely to work with a Hunter group, in my opinion. Changelings and Hunters can work together rather well, feeding the other both info and firepower when needed. Same with Mages. <br /> <br /> Demons are a different story, and far, FAR more likely to manipulate the Hunters to their own ends as proxies in the fight against the God Machine. I wouldn't be surprised if a few Demons have made deals with Hunter Cells to help protect against the Adrians and sniff out Angels. Stigmatic Hunters anyone? Plus demons, no matter how much they try, aren't human and have never been human. Mages are just humans who unlocked fantastic powers. Changelings are people who for the most part try and put their lives back together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T02:29:29-07:00","id":209221,"title":"","content":"Mortal Remains also talks abut how Sin-eaters might help with Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:07:31-07:00","id":209362,"title":"","content":"The Conspiracy I wrote for Dream Catchers has an Endowment that works like Changeling Pledges, and they're renowned for negociation. So not only do they recruit supernaturals they trust their recruits. There's even a sidebar discussing what the Storyteller should do if a player wants to play a Witch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:23:27-07:00","id":209432,"title":"","content":"Dream Catchers? <br /> I've been kicking around the idea of a Changeling focused Conspiracy. Their Endowments come from making deals with Hobgoblins and Exiles, and other creatures of &quot;The Dark Forest&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:34:42-07:00","id":209441,"title":"","content":"It's in my sig. Let me know what you think <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Endowment I wrote is an inverse-Contracts. The idea is to create a foil relationship between the Lord Stewards and Changelings. Both have the same power, but Changelings use promises in deceptive ways (represented by Catches) and Stewards use them with integrity (represented by limitations attached to each power)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T13:09:11-07:00","id":209487,"title":"","content":"Oh lord, you aren't kidding when you say&quot;full length&quot;.<br /> <sub>Man, I really need to work on my fansplat...</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:10:12-07:00","id":209519,"title":"","content":"Vampires have plenty of reason to use mortal dupes (<i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> has the Prince of Berlin actively using the local Hunter cells to hunt for the Strix) for their own purposes; it would make all too much sense to send a bunch of fanatics after your rival instead of risking your own against him. Werewolves might well work with Hunters to deal with pesky spirits, a rival pack, or or the other side of the Forsaken/Pure divide. Mages I'm not so sure about; Hunters are Sleepers and as such, embody the Lie, which makes them tough to use.<br /> <br /> Good luck having a Promethean come up as anything other than something for the cell to kill. The Summer Court of the Changelings may well use Hunters as allies against threats they don't have the manpower to handle, while Autumn might well trade occult lore for pledges. Sin-Eaters aren't terribly antagonistic to begin with, and have plenty of reason to work with Hunters to take down a powerful ghost or necromancer. An Arisen might well manipulate the cell for their own purposes, or might even have a whole Compact/Conspiracy as their Cult. Demons would work freely with Hunters, I'd imagine; Saboteurs get on peachy with them, but Inquisitors might well be interested in their intel and Tempters may well want their souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:35:46-07:00","id":209534,"title":"","content":"I think you've got this thread backwards atamajakki <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Mind you, Sin-Eaters are very easy to recruit, at least on a freelance capacity. They just want money, if you want a ghost gone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T01:13:20-07:00","id":209907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/206438-recruiting-supernaurals?p=209221#post209221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal Remains also talks abut how Sin-eaters might help with Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.. It was mostly about how SEs may work with cells in certain areas but is very, very light on how cells handle SEs who start using ghosts to possess people/torment/etc.<br /> <br /> Granted, SEs are supposed to be like cockroaches because after all, they are tied to Death of all things, but it becomes rather tedious. So I end up digging up the lore of Salt. Salt buckshot does Agg damage to SE while barriers of Salt (powered or stone) prevents them from entering/leaving an area. Also, having the body within a circle of Salt prevents the resurrection process from taking place as long as the body remains there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T22:44:53-07:00","id":212142,"title":"","content":"There's an entire custom Conspiracy that does exactly that. In fact, the head honcho's a True Fae herself. They first investigate any supernatural they find. If it doesn't cause any harm, they might offer a place in the group. But if it does cause harm, then they will deal with it, in a swift and discrete manner.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cardians.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">They are the Cardians, a Family you don't want to cross.</a><br /> <br /> Also, a video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zL4b2DXCPf4\" data-code=\"zL4b2DXCPf4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zL4b2DXCPf4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T11:48:46-07:00","id":219336,"title":"","content":"From the reverse prospective, I just made a mage character that has an allies merit in &quot;Hunters.&quot; My mage is kind of weird because he is pretty proactive in defending sleepers vs. things that go bump in the night so he occasionally works as a pre-cognitive telepathic consultant for The Union while making enchanted weapons for them in return for their agreement to share important information with me from time to time and keep him well equipped with various military grade hardware that includes agg dealing trick bullets that correspond to various antagonists (pure iron, silver, icendiary, blessed, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T20:30:54-07:00","id":223825,"title":"","content":"I once played in a game that had the entire point of being this situation. Everyone began the game as a mortal, who became a Hunter through events in the game. I personally came in later, which wound up being a hoot, because I was a former Marine who got dragged into a bunch of supernatural BULLSH*T and had a tough time believing everything he was seeing at first, conflicting with the other characters who were a bit more well-rooted in the existence of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we all started mortal, then became Hunters -- and <i>then</i>, over a long period of time, we started gaining supernatural templates. Two people Awakened as mages, two people went through their First Change, one person developed a homebrew Psychic major template based on expanded Second Sight powers, one person developed a homebrew Nephilim major template. And I was the guy who wound up being the only mortal of the group by the end of it (debatable, depending on how you interpret the mortality of the Lucifuge), who was almost twice the age of everyone else in the party. Wound up being the mundane-minded straight-man of the group.<br /> <br /> And despite all of these supernatural templates, we <i>stayed</i> Hunters. We still went out and took down crazy supernaturals and dealt with other threats, like burning every last vampire in the city, or dealing with the spirit of the hotel in which we killed all of the vampires of the city -- which had become a murder Magath, because we killed of the vampires of the city inside it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}